@[expose] public section

/-!
# Rational singular cohomology of the circle

The actual two-open cover by punctured circles gives an equivalence from
rational singular H¹ of the circle to ℚ, using the constructed singular
Mayer–Vietoris sequence. Its normalization is the upper-minus-lower
component value on the overlap, and its generator is the connecting image
of the upper-component indicator.

This entry point also exports native homotopy invariance, positive-degree
vanishing for contractible spaces, and degree-zero component coordinates.
-/
